    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0110" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.63/138: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-30T17:00:00+01:00">January 30, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 30—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. I discussed with the German Ambassador today the Austrian-German situation.
                    He is very definite in his statements that Hitler is opposed to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Anschluss</hi> but just as definite in his statement
                    that the Austrian people are German and that the natural development of their
                    political activity will be a government in Austria sympathetic to the German
                    Nazis. He said that he realized that if the Germans participated in the erection
                    of a Nazi state that Italy would not sit complacently and watch it but that he
                    was sure the German Government would not participate. He did not expect any
                    immediate development but thought it would come eventually and in normal
                    course.</p>
                <p>Mailed to Paris, London, Berlin, Vienna, Geneva.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
